; fault_opcode.kasm -- an unassigned encoding, and the code point it reports.
;
; `RDT` with tag 0b111 is the one unassigned tag encoding (spec 8), which makes
; it a compact way to reach ILLEGAL_OPCODE without a wall of `.word`s. A zeroed
; image reaches the same fault, but reports code point 0 -- indistinguishable
; from the RTL's old habit of reporting 0 for every decode fault, so it cannot
; tell a working FAULT_INFO from a broken one.
;
; Written as a `.word` because an assembler that emitted this on request would
; be a bug in the assembler.
; expect: FAULT_ILLEGAL_OPCODE

        .org    0

        .word   0x6c27          ; RDT r1, <unassigned tag>
        halt
